"program_narrative": "Program DB2ONLN is an online (CICS) DB2 connection manager invoked with DB2-REQUEST-AREA that performs one connection operation per call. A connect request (C) checks the active-connection count against the maximum (WS-MAX-CONNECTIONS, initial value 100), issues EXEC SQL CONNECT TO POSMVP, increments the active count and builds a connection token from the current date/time and the count. A disconnect request (D) issues EXEC SQL DISCONNECT and decrements the active count. A status request (S) queries CURRENT SERVER into DB2-ERROR-MSG and returns the active-connection count in DB2-RESPONSE-CODE. The program uses no files; its only external resource is the DB2 connection. Error conditions handled: pool limit reached (-1 with 'Maximum connections reached'), and failed CONNECT, DISCONNECT or status query (-1, with SQLCODE copied to DB2-SQLCODE and, for connect/disconnect, SQLERRMC to DB2-ERROR-MSG); an unrecognised request type performs nothing. Static review notes on P120 token generation and the P300 response-code overwrite are recorded in trace_issues.",
